**Keydown** is the formatting language of [[radii-office|Radii Office]]. Instead of clicking buttons, you type short **tags** around your text, and the text turns into formatting: #G#glossy chips#, %B%gloss pills%, #%O%gel flags%, @neontube-2@unique styles@, =B=gel orbs=B=, #Y#gel highlights##, **bold**, headings, lists and dozens of interactive "applets". Many of its looks come from the [[frutiger-aero|Frutiger Aero]] style. Every example below is drawn live, right on this page.

## How it works

In Writeout and Bitbook, a tag turns into its formatting the moment you press **Space** after it, and pressing **Enter** at the end of a line formats every tag left on that line. In OpenDB, Phosphor and other apps, tags are drawn whenever the text is shown. Most tags wrap your text in an opening and a closing tag, such as `#R#` and `#`. Typing `\\` at the end of a formatted piece steps back out of it.

Writeout and Bitbook can also **Un-format** a whole page, which turns all of its formatting back into tags so mistakes are easy to spot, and **Re-format** it, which formats everything again and underlines any tag that could not be formatted.

Keydown text is saved in `.kd` files (Writeout documents and OpenDB entries) and `.kn` files (Bitbook notes), and those apps can open each other's files.

## Lines

Start a line with one of these and a space:

* `# Heading` makes a big heading, `## Heading` a smaller one and `### Heading` a third level.
* `#### Heading` makes the extra large **mega header**.
* `* item` makes a bullet point, and `> text` a quote.

## Basics

* `**bold**` gives **bold**, and `*italic*` gives *italic*.
* Backticks around a word show it in a `code` font.
* `&&spark&&` gives &&spark&&.

## Gel highlights

The first three tools of the Annotator, as tags: `#R#text##` is a highlight strip, `#R#text#_` a gel underline and `#R#text#~` a gel strike. They come in 13 colors:

* `#R#` red: #R#highlight## #R#underline#_ #R#strike#~
* `#O#` orange: #O#highlight## #O#underline#_ #O#strike#~
* `#GL#` gold: #GL#highlight## #GL#underline#_ #GL#strike#~
* `#Y#` yellow: #Y#highlight## #Y#underline#_ #Y#strike#~
* `#L#` lime: #L#highlight## #L#underline#_ #L#strike#~
* `#G#` green: #G#highlight## #G#underline#_ #G#strike#~
* `#TU#` turquoise: #TU#highlight## #TU#underline#_ #TU#strike#~
* `#T#` teal: #T#highlight## #T#underline#_ #T#strike#~
* `#C#` cyan: #C#highlight## #C#underline#_ #C#strike#~
* `#B#` blue: #B#highlight## #B#underline#_ #B#strike#~
* `#PR#` purple: #PR#highlight## #PR#underline#_ #PR#strike#~
* `#PK#` pink: #PK#highlight## #PK#underline#_ #PK#strike#~
* `#SL#` slate: #SL#highlight## #SL#underline#_ #SL#strike#~

## Bubble chips

Glossy rounded chips, written `#color#text#`:

* `#R#text#` #R#red#
* `#O#text#` #O#orange#
* `#GL#text#` #GL#gold#
* `#Y#text#` #Y#yellow#
* `#L#text#` #L#lime#
* `#G#text#` #G#green#
* `#TU#text#` #TU#turquoise#
* `#T#text#` #T#teal#
* `#C#text#` #C#cyan#
* `#B#text#` #B#blue#
* `#PR#text#` #PR#purple#
* `#PK#text#` #PK#pink#
* `#W#text#` #W#white#
* `#FG#text#` #FG#fog#
* `#SL#text#` #SL#slate#
* `#BK#text#` #BK#black#

## Gloss pills

The Bubble Chips' pill-shaped sibling, with a glassy shine across the top, in the same 16 colors. Written `%color%text%`:

* `%R%text%` %R%red%
* `%O%text%` %O%orange%
* `%GL%text%` %GL%gold%
* `%Y%text%` %Y%yellow%
* `%L%text%` %L%lime%
* `%G%text%` %G%green%
* `%TU%text%` %TU%turquoise%
* `%T%text%` %T%teal%
* `%C%text%` %C%cyan%
* `%B%text%` %B%blue%
* `%PR%text%` %PR%purple%
* `%PK%text%` %PK%pink%
* `%W%text%` %W%white%
* `%FG%text%` %FG%fog%
* `%SL%text%` %SL%slate%
* `%BK%text%` %BK%black%

## Gel flags

Another Bubble Chip cousin: the same gel, flowing sideways from a thick colored edge. Written `#%color%text%`:

* `#%R%text%` #%R%red%
* `#%O%text%` #%O%orange%
* `#%GL%text%` #%GL%gold%
* `#%Y%text%` #%Y%yellow%
* `#%L%text%` #%L%lime%
* `#%G%text%` #%G%green%
* `#%TU%text%` #%TU%turquoise%
* `#%T%text%` #%T%teal%
* `#%C%text%` #%C%cyan%
* `#%B%text%` #%B%blue%
* `#%PR%text%` #%PR%purple%
* `#%PK%text%` #%PK%pink%
* `#%W%text%` #%W%white%
* `#%FG%text%` #%FG%fog%
* `#%SL%text%` #%SL%slate%
* `#%BK%text%` #%BK%black%

## Gel orbs

Round glossy orbs, written `=color=text=color=`:

* `=Y=text=Y=` =Y=yellow=Y=
* `=R=text=R=` =R=red=R=
* `=G=text=G=` =G=green=G=
* `=C=text=C=` =C=cyan=C=
* `=B=text=B=` =B=blue=B=
* `=V=text=V=` =V=violet=V=
* `=P=text=P=` =P=pink=P=
* `=O=text=O=` =O=orange=O=
* `=MG=text=MG=` =MG=magenta=MG=
* `=LM=text=LM=` =LM=lime=LM=
* `=AQ=text=AQ=` =AQ=aqua=AQ=
* `=SL=text=SL=` =SL=slate=SL=

## Tag chips

A Bubble Chip cousin shaped like a luggage tag, with a little eyelet hole, in the same 16 colors. Written `!#color#text#`:

* `!#R#text#` !#R#red#
* `!#O#text#` !#O#orange#
* `!#GL#text#` !#GL#gold#
* `!#Y#text#` !#Y#yellow#
* `!#L#text#` !#L#lime#
* `!#G#text#` !#G#green#
* `!#TU#text#` !#TU#turquoise#
* `!#T#text#` !#T#teal#
* `!#C#text#` !#C#cyan#
* `!#B#text#` !#B#blue#
* `!#PR#text#` !#PR#purple#
* `!#PK#text#` !#PK#pink#
* `!#W#text#` !#W#white#
* `!#FG#text#` !#FG#fog#
* `!#SL#text#` !#SL#slate#
* `!#BK#text#` !#BK#black#

## Text effects

* `~G~text~G~` Gel green flash: ~G~Sample~G~
* `~U~text~U~` Liquid underline: ~U~Sample~U~
* `~B~text~B~` Glossy border badge: ~B~Sample~B~
* `~S~text~S~` Cyber glow spark: ~S~Sample~S~
* `~L~text~L~` Liquid text glow: ~L~Sample~L~
* `~M~text~M~` Reflected text block: ~M~Sample~M~
* `~E~text~E~` Embossed glass text: ~E~Sample~E~
* `~W~text~W~` Kinetic wave text: ~W~Sample~W~

The older line tags `~H1~`, `~H2~`, `~H3~`, `~MH~`, `~BQ~` and `~BUL~` still work, but the line shortcuts above are easier.

## Applets

Applets are small interactive widgets: click the ones below to try them. Wrap a label in the tag:

* `~FN~label~FN~` Foldout tab: ~FN~Demo~FN~
* `~TS~label~TS~` Aqua switch: ~TS~Demo~TS~
* `~SM~label~SM~` Glass stamp: ~SM~Demo~SM~
* `~TB~label~TB~` State button (green): ~TB~Demo~TB~
