## Blocks

A line that is only `::name` becomes a whole block, such as a glass panel, a code box or a divider. Put your own text in curly braces after the name, like `::glass{Welcome aboard}`. Blocks with a title and a body take both, split by `|`, like `::foldout{Packing list|Socks, a map and snacks}`, and in `::code`, `::console` and `::diff` every `|` starts a new line.

`::glass{Welcome aboard}`

::glass{Welcome aboard}

`::bubble{Floating note}`

::bubble{Floating note}

`::alert{Check your spelling!}`

::alert{Check your spelling!}

`::media{NOW PLAYING: Ocean Waves.wav}`

::media{NOW PLAYING: Ocean Waves.wav}

`::aqua{Ideas for the weekend}`

::aqua{Ideas for the weekend}

`::code{let total = 0|total = total + 1}`

::code{let total = 0|total = total + 1}

`::emerald{Garden plans}`

::emerald{Garden plans}

`::amber{Best moments}`

::amber{Best moments}

`::crimson{Due on Friday}`

::crimson{Due on Friday}

`::amethyst{Story drafts}`

::amethyst{Story drafts}

`::gsky{Sky notes|Clear skies all week}`

::gsky{Sky notes|Clear skies all week}

`::gemerald{Eco notes|Plant three trees}`

::gemerald{Eco notes|Plant three trees}

`::gamber{Highlights|The demo went well}`

::gamber{Highlights|The demo went well}

`::gcrimson{Warnings|Back up your files}`

::gcrimson{Warnings|Back up your files}

`::foldout{Packing list|Socks, a map and snacks}`

